Test the microphone recorded with Windows' conversion

WebRTC patch 0013 records a capture device that takes none of the formats
AudioDeviceWindowsCore::InitRecording tries at 48 kHz, with Windows' audio engine
converting from the device's mix format. test/capture_conversion.test.cc (Windows only)
takes that path for the computer's first capture device
(InitRecordingWithConversionForTesting), records half a second and checks that 10 ms
blocks arrive at 48 kHz in the channels chosen. Without a capture device it is skipped.

